{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3515","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3515","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3515\",\"parent_revision\":\"a443cc5c2f0939a6d2ceca8085cd32ce50aeec3d7582142fdb38a9be692c0f24\",\"root_revision\":\"a443cc5c2f0939a6d2ceca8085cd32ce50aeec3d7582142fdb38a9be692c0f24\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Docs\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-09-13\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nPR #3514 added `.claude/skills/research-curator/references/entry-review-rubric.md` \u2014 a six-gate audit of a finished research entry and its improvement/utilization files \u2014 plus three other new references (`entry-quality-standards.md`, `extraction-methodology.md`, `cross-reference-format.md`).\\n\\n`.claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md` was held by another agent during that session and could not be edited, so the rubric is not wired into the workflow. Consequence: the Default, Batch, and Rerun modes all proceed from waiting on the analysis tasks straight into Post-Actions (lint, commit, push). No orchestrator or agent is instructed to run the six gates, so an entry and its insight/utilization files can be committed and pushed with the audit never having executed. The skill's Reference Links section also never names the rubric or the three other new references, so nothing discovers them from SKILL.md.\\n\\nImpact: the rubric exists but does not run. The defects it was written to catch \u2014 unverified repo claims in insight files, generic repo analysis, speculation language, missing per-severity validator counts \u2014 continue to reach merged PRs, which is the condition that prompted writing it (a review of PR #3510 had to invent a rubric from scratch).\\n\\nTwo edits are needed in SKILL.md:\\n\\n1. Reference Links section (currently ends with the `[Repo Access Procedure]` line, around line 540) \u2014 add entries for `entry-quality-standards.md`, `extraction-methodology.md`, `entry-review-rubric.md`, and `cross-reference-format.md`.\\n\\n2. Default Mode flow \u2014 insert a review step between step 7 (\\\"Wait for all tasks above and surface results\\\", around line 166) and the current step 8 (\\\"Post-actions\\\"), renumbering the rest: audit the entry and any insight/utilization files written this run against the rubric, report each gate's verdict and every defect, and do not proceed to Post-Actions with an unresolved defect. Batch Mode and Rerun Mode reach Post-Actions on their own paths and need the same gate.\\n\\nUser-provided context: exact suggested wording for both edits is in the PR #3514 description under \\\"Follow-ups blocked by locked files\\\", and was messaged to the agent holding SKILL.md.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Codex review on PR #3514 (.claude/skills/research-curator/references/entry-review-rubric.md:5)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-13\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"e899f240a5c7c389a653e3332e62a3621ad4125154da84667bb78c11c756de93\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABUPu5zQ\"}"}